Z||000006||rockcrawl||01-28-2001||07:08 PM||||The crossfire was used in '82-'84 F-bodies and '82,'84 vettes. Why anyone would use the Crossfire ECM to run the Northstar is beyond me. I'm sure it's becuase it's easier to hack than a N* ECM, but all the Crossfire guys are swapping out thier ECMs for the faster/easier to hack '7747 ECM from the full-size trucks. The X-fire has a slow processing rate. Actually the 5 liter X-fire ECM would probably run the N* just fine without any mods, but performance would be lacking I'm sure.<P>BTW, my Jeep has a crossfire 305 from an '82 Camaro. It's better than any carbuerator and cheaper than TPI or Pro-jection.<P>------------------<BR>Jon Lagler<BR>'87 GT<BR>4.9 liter V8 Testarossa Spyder (under construction)<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/rockcrawlsig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
